Z||000003||RFMike||06-15-99||11:01 PM||||I agree.  If you want the fastest, straight line screamer on the block, you bought the wrong car.  That said, there are a lot of things these cars do very well.  One of them is, indeed, turning heads.  Another is cruising through a tight turn, at the car's grip limit, knowing that there are other cars out there that will do it better, but not by much, and for a lot more dough.  This all goes back to the original design intent of this car, which was to satisfy an overly broad segment of buyers.  Remember, this was called a "two seat commuter" at different times in its promotion.  Considering how diluted it could have been, its damn near a miracle its as good as it is.<p>All right, I'm off the soapbox.  Just trying to say, enjoy it for what it is- a pretty well rounded sports car, unique to itself.  As another person said in a different thread, "it is what it is." 
Z||000004||Motorhead||06-16-99||03:48 AM||||Mike hit it on the head!<p>Your Fiero does what it was intended to do very well!  <p>My other "Toy" is a Datsun 280ZX, extremely fast, but lacking my Fieros' finese through the turns!<p>Enjoy the car for what it is.  If you want to go street racing, get a different car!<br>
Z||000005||batboy||06-16-99||08:46 AM||||I too agree with the comments being expressed here. I've had a 87 SE 4 cylinder for about 3 years and love it. It truly is my commuter car (who wants to drive an pathetic econo-box to work every day), but it's also fun to drive (and the ladies love it too). Sure, lots of expensive riceburners pick on me, but I don't want to trade 35 miles per gallon for anything. So, I bought a second Fiero with a V8 conversion. Just a couple days ago when I was driving my hotrod Fiero, some butt-munch passed three cars at once and flipped me the bird as he went by. I easily caught up with him on the next curve (he had to brake and I didn't). I eased up next to him on the straight at 80 mph plus, then punched it. I just walked away from him like he was standing still. Even my SS 396 Chevelle I had in my youth couldn't of done that. It took all evening to wipe the grin off my face. I can still remember that shocked look on the other guys face as I passed him.
Z||000006||lowCG||06-16-99||01:59 PM||||Ha! He probably went to the nearest Pontiac dealer he could find!
Z||000007||Racer 1||06-16-99||04:58 PM||||One other thing to remeber is the fiero is over 11 years old.If "FREAKING" pontaic would have kept on building and improving the fiero.We might have gotten a supercharged engine or a Quad 4 HO engine.Dangit now im getting depressed thinking about what coulda been a racer against the MR-2.Technology has come along way since 1988.Lets all go picket pontaic headquaters till they make the fiero again???   8-) 
Z||000008||PaUL||06-16-99||07:07 PM||||Pontiac make the fiero again? No way, they wont do it. GM stopped making brand specific platforms in the 80s. By that I mean platforms that arent shared with other divisions like the Buick Reatta and Cadillac Allante. The only one that remains is the Corvette. They did this to save money and thats the bottom line, they cant turn a big enough profit to produce a unique car limited to one division. 
Z||000009||Hock||07-02-99||02:27 PM||||What is wrong with you people? The Fiero is one of the best street cars I have ever known, driven, or have rode in. I can't believe that any of you would give up on it as a street racer. I have gotten betten several times by these damn junk rice burners, but you don't see me throwing in the towel. Do you? NO, I am taking the time and the money buying another Fiero and rebuilding my 2.5 and am going to go out and kick some import ass. This has been along time coming. Everytime I get pasted up by a Neon, Eclipse, or any other little rice burner I get even madder. The Fiero is a true American performance car, even if its a little short from the start, the can be made in to one of the fastest. How many rice burners do any of you know of that can go right from the 1/4 mile straight to a 90 degree turn? None that I know of. I haven't found one rice burner yet that could out handle my Fiero, not one. And when I get it done I garantee that there will not be any that will. And thats the bottom line, because I said so.<br>                    HOCK
