Z||000012||87GT||07-02-99||07:57 PM||||The coolest thing happened today.  I was coming down US 301 in Dade City and came up on a identical twin to my car.  I pulled up next to the other Fiero to find that a chic was driving it.  (She looked good too).  Anyways,  She thought it was cool that I had a car just like hers, so we stayed side by side all the way into Dade City and we got some goofy looks. I thought it was so awesome. Anyways, we waved at each other to say bye once we had to go our different ways.  She didnt have the Ferrari like side scoops that mine has, I think that was the only difference.  I just drive my car because it is fun to drive, and when I need it to get up and go, it does it!  Plus, the car is stunning to look at.  This is why I like Fieros so much. 8-)
Z||000013||Hock||07-03-99||10:50 AM||||I am glad to see that there are other people out there that love to keep it going. I mean never die, never give up. Thats the way it has been since this great country was founded. Never once have we as a nation put down our guns to in the face of opposition. We have never let any other country get away with trying to take over our land. So why stop now? Even if we are taking about cars and our stupid competion with these rice burners and German cars, we still have the thing that matters most, American Pride. And as long as we keep that there will be nothing that will defeat us. NOTHING! Yes, we may have lost a couple of battles along the way but, we will win the war on the streets. This is for certain.
